INT. FREIGHT ELEVATOR, CANNERY - NIGHT

Steel cage. Flickering bulb. Stuck between floors.

SAUL VERHOEVEN (50s, grey suit, bleeding sleeve) leans on the wall. NADIA PRUITT (30s, tactical vest, gun lowered) watches the hatch. Beside her, a young courier, EMEKA OSEI (20s, backpack hugged tight).

NADIA
(to everyone)
Nobody touches the panel.

EMEKA
(quiet, to Saul)
Is it bad? Your arm?

SAUL
It's fine, kid.

Nadia cranes toward the ceiling. Dust drifts down.

NADIA
(under her breath)
Come on, come on. Not now.

Boots thump overhead. Then stop. Then nothing.

EMEKA
They're gone?

NADIA
(to Emeka)
Be still.

Saul slides the backpack from Emeka's arms. Emeka lets him.

SAUL
(to himself)
Should've taken the stairs.

The cage lurches. Slowly, it starts to rise.
